256:.portrait { width: 148px; height: 148px; position: relative; z-index: 2; color: var(--titan); filter: drop-shadow(0 0 22px color-mix(in srgb, var(--titan) 32%, transparent)); }
347:.hud { position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; }
485:  position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 80;
557:.toasts { position: fixed; right: 20px; top: 86px; z-index: 90; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; pointer-events: none; width: min(320px, 70vw); }
576:  position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 70; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
597:  z-index: 65; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(30px, 5vw, 62px);
608:.action-flash { position: fixed; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; z-index: 4; }
609:.cinematic-bars { position: fixed; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; z-index: 40; }

Menu is z-index 200, so mobile controls below menu. Fine. Overlay z-index 80, also above mobile controls? mobile-controls has no z-index, within #ui z-index 10. So overlays above. Good. We can add visible on narrow safely; it will be under menu/overlays.

But the `#ui` has pointer-events none; mobile buttons have pointer-events auto via `.mob-btn`. Good.

Let's update JS:
```
const mobileQuery = window.matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)');
const updateMobile = () => this.mobileControls.classList.toggle('visible', mobileQuery.matches || window.innerWidth <= 760);
...
```
Replace the existing `if (window.matchMedia...)`. Also add resize listener. Use `this._mobileQuery` maybe.

Then CSS reposition mobile actions/joystick to avoid player card:
```
@media (max-width: 760px) {
  .joystick { left: 14px; bottom: 160px; width: 116px; height: 116px; }
  .mobile-actions { right: 10px; bottom: 104px; width: 210px; gap: 6px; }
