}
for (const beam of this.activeBeams) {
  ...
  if (perBeam) {
    beam.tick = (beam.tick ?? 0) - dt;
    if (beam.tick <= 0) {
      beam.tick = sp.beamTick ?? 0.12;
      this.game.beamDamage(...)
    }
  } else if (a.tick <= 0) {
    a.tick = sp.beamTick ?? 0.12;
    this.game.beamDamage(...)
  }
}
```
Wait for non-per-beam, we decrement `a.tick` once per frame, then loop; first beam triggers and sets a.tick = interval. Subsequent beams skip. Good.
For per-beam, decrement each beam.tick; each triggers independently. Good.

Add data `beamPerBeamTick: true` to Ghidorah, and set beamDamage back to 0.12 (per beam). Total: 52*0.12=6.24 per beam per tick × 3 × 27 = 505. Similar to 0.36 global (486 observed). Good. Actually 6.24*3=18.72 per tick, 27 ticks = 505. Good.
